# day 15 · piece 1 of 1 — lib.sh: five functions, meant to be sourced
#
# Two rules the checker enforces: every working variable is `local` (it diffs the
# global namespace before and after calling you), and a function returns DATA on
# stdout or a STATUS via return — never both by accident. The #RUN sources the file
# into a fresh bash and calls each function; the stubs below all do nothing, so every
# line comes back empty and `contains z` wrongly reports 0. Fill them in one at a time
# and save after each — the OUTPUT pane is your unit test, the CHECK pane the grader.
#DAY 15
#FILE lib.sh
